    "notes": {
      "paths": "all three paths interpolate their names raw — `list` and `create` the identifier alias, `rename` both the alias and the registry name — so none of the four dynamic values is encoded",
      "backers": "`noBackers` defaults to **true**, so an ordinary creation writes the `NB` configuration trait and the backer list and threshold it also accepts are never used",
      "est_only": "an establishment-only identifier pushes the `EO` trait into the configuration, builds the registry inception with it, and *then* throws `establishment only not implemented` — so the work is done and discarded",
      "result": "`RegistryResult` holds the fetch **promise**, not its response, so `create` returns before the POST resolves and a failure is invisible unless `op()` is awaited"
    }
